Add AI-upscaled hires background override for the overhead/travel map.

Rationale: TattooMap::show() bypasses Scene::loadScene() entirely and uses
its own larger, double-size scrollable canvas, so it never picked up a
Rose Tattoo hires background override (see
rosetattoo-hires-map-black-screen-fix.patch, which just clears the stale
room-sized override so update() falls back to a plain nearest-neighbor
scale-up instead of crashing/rendering garbled). That earlier fix restored
correct scaling but left the map itself looking blocky/low-res, unlike
every normal room background.

This factors the existing scene-background-override decode logic in
Screen::loadRoseTattooHiresBackgroundOverride() into a shared
loadRoseTattooHiresBackgroundFromPath() helper, then adds a sibling
Screen::loadRoseTattooHiresMapOverride() that looks for a fixed
"sprites/map_vgs/frame_000@<scale>x.png" override path (matching the
extract_rosetattoo_sprites.py/upscale_rosetattoo_sprites.py naming
convention already used for the MAP.VGS resource) instead of a per-scene
one. TattooMap::show() calls it right after resizing _backBuffer1 to the
map's own dimensions, since the expected override size is derived from
_backBuffer1 at call time - this made the existing size-validation logic
work unmodified for the map's much larger canvas.

The corresponding hires map asset itself (a real ESRGAN super-resolution
upscale of MAP.VGS + MAP.PAL, extracted via extract_rosetattoo_sprites.py
--palette-resource MAP.PAL) is generated by tooling, not part of this
engine patch.

